          "lineage": "Psephenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "description": "Adult male (Figs. 20, 21): body oblong-ovate, rather broad, depressed, dorsum shining, densely pubescent. Head profusely rugulose, vertex foveate, dorsal concavity not divided. Elytra oblong, little wider than thorax; pronotal sides strongly convergent anteriorly, apex not more than half as wide as base. Maxillary palp threequarters length of antenna, second segment of maxillary palp usually longer than third and fourth combined. Male genitalia (Figs. 22, 23): apex of median penial spicule enlarged and bluntly rounded.",
